<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      strategy_defaults row for Strategy 7 (STRATEGIES.md, "Strategy 7").

      Why a changeset and not an operator INSERT
      ==========================================
      Strategy 7 is Strategy 6 plus the first-hour gate, and its measured edge
      (STRATEGY_ANALYSIS_TODO.md S28) was replayed on the SAME strategy_defaults
      block strategy 1 runs on - transaction_type SELL, the same max_loss,
      no_of_trades and no_of_parallel_trades - just as Strategy 6's was (046).
      So the block is copied from strategy 1, which also means the strategies
      share ONE generated config row (configSignature) and appear as "1,6,7"
      on it, exactly the shape the replay measured.

      What it does NOT do
      ===================
      It does not tag strategy 7 on any sma_downtrend_rule, so nothing trades
      until an operator says so (CLAUDE.md Rule 0(c)). Switching it on is one
      row per rule:

          INSERT INTO sma_downtrend_rule_strategy (rule_id, strategy_id, enabled)
          SELECT rs.rule_id, 7, TRUE
            FROM sma_downtrend_rule_strategy rs
           WHERE rs.strategy_id = 1 AND rs.enabled = TRUE;

      Idempotent and order-safe: a no-op when strategy 7 already has a row, and
      a no-op on a database that has no strategy 1 row yet (fresh install before
      the operator seeds strategy 1 - then insert 7 by hand the same way, see
      docs/EOD_DOWNTREND.md "strategy_defaults"). opposite_side is FALSE: like 1
      and 2 it sells the leg the downtrend was detected on. target_mode /
      sl_mode (changeset 041) are copied too, so 7 brackets exactly as 1 does.
    -->
    <changeSet id="047_seed_strategy7_defaults" author="moneymaker">
        <sql>
            INSERT INTO strategy_defaults
                (strategy_id, transaction_type, lot_quantity, max_loss,
                 no_of_trades, no_of_parallel_trades, auto_config_enabled, opposite_side,
                 target_mode, sl_mode)
            SELECT 7, s.transaction_type, s.lot_quantity, s.max_loss,
                   s.no_of_trades, s.no_of_parallel_trades, s.auto_config_enabled, FALSE,
                   s.target_mode, s.sl_mode
              FROM strategy_defaults s
             WHERE s.strategy_id = 1
               AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM strategy_defaults x WHERE x.strategy_id = 7)
        </sql>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
